This directory contains a number of sample QuIDDPro scripts which
simulate a variety of quantum computational and communications
applications.  More scripts will be added in future releases.

Subdirectories
--------------

errs: Contains scripts which simulate errors and error correction for
      various quantum circuits.  Please see our related paper which
      can be found at http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0403114

functions: Contains scripts which demonstrate user-defined functions

misc: Contains various scripts ranging from instances of Grover's
      quantum search algorithm to canonical two-qubit decomposition.

nist: Contains scripts which implement some of NIST's QCSim
      bencharmks.  Please see our related paper which can be found at
      http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0403114

qtf: Contains scripts which implement the Quantum Fourier Transform.

phase_checks: Contains scripts which demonstrate the efficient
              global and relative phase equivalence checking functions.
              These functions also compute the phase factors.

rand_cnot: Contains randomly generated scripts which simulate 1000 CNOT
           gates on circuits with 200 qubits.  A program to generate
           these random circuits is included.

rand_toff: Contains randomly generated scripts which simulate 
           1000 Toffoli gates on circuits with 200 qubits. A program
           to generate these random circuits is included.

rev: Contains scripts which simulate a variety of reversible logic
     circuits with and without errors and error correction.  Please
     see our related paper which can be found at
     http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0403114

run: Contains scripts which demonstrate the run command

stabilizer_circuits: Contains scripts which simulate some of the
		     sample circuits bundled with Scott Aaronson's
		     CHP stabilizer circuit simulator.  A program to
		     convert CHP circuits to QuIDDPro scripts is also
		     included.

states: Contains QuIDDPro scripts which demonstrate the Dirac-style
        syntax and a few string manipulation features.

toff_stabilizer_circuits: Contains a QuIDDPro script which simulates
                          Toffoli gates and stabilizer gates on
                          a random circuit with 100 qubits. A program to
                          generate these circuits is included.

